## qf-sci | Quick-fire: science | physics | 0 | - | ph-odd
quiz 2 | What's the SI unit of electric charge?
* Coulomb
o Ampere
o Volt
o Ohm
= One coulomb is one ampere flowing for one second.
> Next

quiz 2 | Speed of light in vacuum, to 1 significant figure?
* 3 × 10⁸ m/s
o 3 × 10⁶ m/s
o 3 × 10¹⁰ m/s
o 3 × 10⁵ m/s
= Exactly 299,792,458 m/s, by definition of the metre since 1983.
> Next

quiz 2 | Which particle has no electric charge?
* Neutron
o Proton
o Electron
o Positron
= Chadwick discovered it in 1932.
> Next

quiz 3 | What does a joule per second equal?
* A watt
o A newton
o A volt
o A pascal
= Power is energy per unit time.
> Next

quiz 3 | Absolute zero in Celsius?
* −273.15°C
o −100°C
o −459.67°C
o −373.15°C
= −459.67 is the Fahrenheit value.
> Next

quiz 3 | What colour of visible light has the longest wavelength?
* Red
o Violet
o Green
o Blue
= Around 700 nm. Violet is around 400 nm.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which force holds protons together in a nucleus despite their repulsion?
* The strong nuclear force
o Gravity
o The weak force
o Magnetism
= It's the strongest force, but acts only over about 10⁻¹⁵ m.
> Next

quiz 3 | Sound travels fastest through…
* Steel
o Air
o Water
o A vacuum
= About 5,900 m/s in steel, 1,480 in water, 343 in air. None in a vacuum.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is the approximate acceleration due to gravity on Earth's surface?
* 9.8 m/s²
o 6.7 m/s²
o 1.6 m/s²
o 98 m/s²
= 1.6 m/s² is the Moon's.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which planet has the shortest day?
* Jupiter
o Mercury
o Earth
o Saturn
= About 9 hours 56 minutes, despite being the largest planet.
