## qf-maths | Quick-fire: maths | maths | 0 | - | mt-geo
quiz 2 | What is 0! (zero factorial)?
* 1
o 0
o Undefined
o ∞
= There's exactly one way to arrange nothing. It also makes formulas like n!/(n − k)! work.
> Next

quiz 2 | Sum of the interior angles of a hexagon?
* 720°
o 360°
o 540°
o 1080°
= (n − 2) × 180°.
> Next

quiz 3 | What is i²?
* −1
o 1
o i
o 0
= By definition.
> Next

quiz 3 | How many edges does a cube have?
* 12
o 8
o 6
o 24
= Euler: V − E + F = 8 − 12 + 6 = 2.
> Next

quiz 3 | log₂(1024) = ?
* 10
o 8
o 12
o 512
= 2¹⁰ = 1024.
> Next

quiz 3 | The derivative of a constant is…
* 0
o 1
o The constant
o Undefined
= Constants don't change.
> Next

quiz 3 | How many ways can you arrange 5 different books on a shelf?
* 120
o 25
o 60
o 5
= 5! = 120.
> Next

quiz 3 | How many ways to choose 2 people from 10?
* 45
o 90
o 20
o 100
= 10C2 = 10 × 9/2.
> Next

quiz 3 | What's the next prime after 89?
* 97
o 91
o 93
o 99
= 91 = 7 × 13, 93 = 3 × 31, 95 = 5 × 19.
> Next

quiz 4 | What's the probability of rolling at least one six in four rolls of a die?
* About 52%
o About 67%
o About 25%
o About 48%
= 1 − (5/6)⁴ ≈ 0.518. This bet made money for the Chevalier de Méré in the 1600s.
> More quick-fire next

## qf-hist | Quick-fire: history | history | 0 | - | wo-cult
quiz 2 | In which year did the Berlin Wall fall?
* 1989
o 1991
o 1961
o 1979
= 9 November 1989. Germany reunified in October 1990.
