quiz 2 | Who was the first person in space?
* Yuri Gagarin
o Neil Armstrong
o Alan Shepard
o Valentina Tereshkova
= 12 April 1961, one orbit, 108 minutes.
= Tereshkova was the first woman, in 1963.
> Next

quiz 3 | The Battle of Hastings was in…
* 1066
o 1215
o 1415
o 1666
= William of Normandy defeated Harold II. 1215 is Magna Carta.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which empire built Machu Picchu?
* The Inca
o The Aztec
o The Maya
o The Olmec
= Built around the mid-1400s, high in the Andes.
> Next

quiz 3 | Who wrote The Communist Manifesto (1848)?
* Marx and Engels
o Lenin
o Trotsky
o Rousseau
= Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels.
> Next

quiz 3 | The Great Fire of London was in…
* 1666
o 1066
o 1766
o 1566
= It burned for about four days and destroyed most of the medieval City.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which ancient wonder still stands?
* The Great Pyramid of Giza
o The Colossus of Rhodes
o The Hanging Gardens of Babylon
o The Lighthouse of Alexandria
= The oldest of the seven, and the only one left.
> Next

quiz 3 | Who was the first female Prime Minister of the UK?
* Margaret Thatcher
o Theresa May
o Barbara Castle
o Liz Truss
= 1979 to 1990.
> Next

quiz 4 | The Rosetta Stone is in which museum?
* The British Museum
o The Louvre
o The Egyptian Museum, Cairo
o The Metropolitan Museum
= It has been in London since 1802. Egypt has requested its return.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which came first: the printing press or the compass in Europe?
* The compass (in Europe by about 1190)
o The printing press
o Same decade
= Magnetic compasses were used in Chinese navigation by about 1100 and in Europe by the late 1100s. Gutenberg's press: around 1450.
