quiz 2 | How many chromosomes do humans normally have?
* 46
o 23
o 48
o 44
= 23 pairs.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which blood type is the "universal donor" for red cells?
* O negative
o AB positive
o A negative
o B positive
= It lacks A, B and RhD antigens. AB positive is the universal recipient.
> Next

quiz 3 | What's the largest organ of the human body?
* The skin
o The liver
o The brain
o The lungs
= Around 2 m² in adults. The liver is the largest internal organ.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which animal has the largest brain?
* The sperm whale
o The elephant
o The blue whale
o The human
= About 8 kg. Humans have one of the largest brains relative to body size.
> Next

quiz 3 | What molecule carries oxygen in your red blood cells?
* Haemoglobin
o Myoglobin
o Insulin
o Collagen
= Each haemoglobin molecule carries up to four oxygen molecules.
> Next

quiz 3 | Which vitamin does your skin make in sunlight?
* Vitamin D
o Vitamin C
o Vitamin A
o Vitamin B12
= UVB light converts a cholesterol derivative in the skin.
> Next

quiz 4 | Which of these is NOT a mammal?
* Shark
o Whale
o Bat
o Platypus
= Sharks are fish. The platypus is an egg-laying mammal.
> Next

quiz 3 | How many hearts does an octopus have?
* 3
o 1
o 2
o 8
= Two for the gills, one for the body.
> Next

quiz 4 | Tardigrades can survive…
* All of these, in their dried "tun" state
o Near absolute zero
o Thousands of times normal atmospheric pressure
o The vacuum of space
= Extreme tolerance, though active tardigrades are much more fragile.
